> Actual source performance

These are the original ten-run comparison averages. The first plot shows the first ten episodes for0,5,50 planning updates per real step. The second uses the original changing-maze runs; the wall gap switches at real step1000. The separate final playback run is excluded from these averages.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/dyna_q_diagnostic0.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -lpthread -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){auto data=dm::nn::load_npz("build/dyna_q_source.npz");auto lookup=[&](const std::string&key){return std::find_if(data.begin(),data.end(),[&](const auto&v){return v.first==key;})->second.to_vector<double>();};auto plot=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();for(int group=0;group<3;++group){std::vector<double>x(10),y(10,0);std::iota(x.begin(),x.end(),1.);for(int run=0;run<10;++run){auto v=lookup("episodes_"+std::to_string(group*10+run));for(size_t i=0;i<std::min(size_t(10),v.size());++i)y[i]+=v[i]/10;}plot.lines(x,y,"planning steps="+std::to_string(group==0?0:group==1?5:50),{37+group*70,99,235-group*70});}plot.x_label("Ended episode").y_label("Mean real steps, ten original runs");plot.title("Dyna-Q original comparison averages").size(1100,600).save_svg("build/dyna_q_diagnostic0.svg");}
